Doctor: Command owner
│
◇  Command owner ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                          │
│  No channel command owner is configured.                                 │
│  A command owner is your trusted human operator account, allowed to      │
│  update OpenClaw with /update, restart the Gateway, change               │
│  configuration, and approve commands. Chat allowlists do not grant this  │
│  authority.                                                              │
│  Local Control UI/WebChat clients with operator.admin already have       │
│  owner authority; no channel is required. Run openclaw --profile         │
│  proof124337 dashboard on the Gateway host and open its link in your     │
│  browser (use openclaw --profile proof124337 dashboard --json on a       │
│  headless host).                                                         │
│  If the Control UI shows limited access, open Inbox > System > Limited   │
│  access > Request admin, then run its displayed openclaw --profile       │
│  proof124337 devices approve <requestId> command on the Gateway host.    │
│  For external channels, run openclaw --profile proof124337 channels add  │
│  and complete a channel's setup to choose your operator account,         │
│  including servers and groups without DM pairing.                        │
│  CLI channel pairing approval records the first command owner. Control   │
│  UI channel-sender approval has a separate owner checkbox.               │
│  For an existing channel sender, set commands.ownerAllowFrom to your     │
│  channel user id, for example openclaw --profile proof124337 config set  │
│  commands.ownerAllowFrom '["telegram:123456789"]'                        │
│  Restart the Gateway after changing commands.ownerAllowFrom if it is     │
│  already running.                                                        │
│                                                                          │
